-## 2. Versioning Model
+## 2. Rate Limiting Configuration
+
+The gateway reads rate limiting settings from `config/gateway.conf` at startup. Edit the `G_GATEWAY_CONF` values and rebuild the gateway for changes to take effect. Global settings are the default for API versions that do not have an explicit policy.
+
+```c
+.rate_limit_enabled        = true,
+.rate_limit_requests       = 100,
+.rate_limit_window_seconds = 60
+```
+
+Version-specific policies are configured in `G_VERSION_RATE_LIMITS`:
+
+```c
+VERSION_RL("v1", 60, 60),
+VERSION_RL("v2", 500, 60)
+```
+
+These correspond to:
+
+```ini
+rate_limit_v1 = 60:60
+rate_limit_v2 = 500:60
+```
+
+| Key | Type | Description |
+|-----|------|-------------|
+| `rate_limit_enabled` | `true` / `false` | Enables or disables request throttling. When disabled, all requests bypass the limiter. |
+| `rate_limit_requests` | integer | Default maximum number of requests allowed per client IP in one window. |
+| `rate_limit_window_seconds` | integer | Default length of the rate-limit window in seconds. |
+
+When a client exceeds the configured quota, the gateway returns **429 Too Many Requests** with:
+
+```json
+{ "error": "Rate limit exceeded" }
+```
+
+---
+
